   248	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   249	    """
   250	    Split foreground objects into solid complete squares, hollow complete squares, and non-squares, then mark each branch differently.
   251	
   252	    Input structure:
   253	    - Black background with several 4-connected monochrome foreground objects in non-red colors.
   254	    - Some objects are complete squares: their bounding boxes are square and every bbox-border cell belongs to the object.
   255	    - Complete squares may be solid or may surround one or more enclosed black holes; other objects are irregular distractors.
   256	
   257	    Rule:
   258	    - Find each 4-connected foreground component and test whether it is a complete square by the component's own bbox and border pixels.
   259	    - For complete squares only, test whether any black background region inside the bbox interior is enclosed and cannot reach the grid boundary.
   260	    - Solid complete squares keep their color and receive red orthogonal corner-outside marks; hollow complete squares are recolored teal, their enclosed holes are filled pink, and then a red 8-neighbor outline is drawn around the filled shape; non-square objects keep their color and only receive that red outline.

